<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phalsbourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1570">1570</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Pfalzburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phalsbourg (German Pfalzburg) is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the road across the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>. It was founded in 1570 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-john-i-count-palatine-of-veldenz">George John I, Count Palatine of Veldenz</a>, and named after the Palatinate, but was sold to the Duke of Lorraine in 1583. Under French rule it was fortified by Vauban and became a garrison town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phalsbourg.jpg" alt="Phalsbourg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raimond Spekking · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotel_de_ville_de_Phalsbourg-9708.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
